You're so kind, Paul.
保罗，你太好了。

933
00:46:15.400 --> 00:46:18.440
I mean, the majority of the writers think it was you.
我是说，大多数编剧都觉得是你的。

934
00:46:18.660 --> 00:46:18.860
Okay.
好吧。

935
00:46:18.860 --> 00:46:21.180
But you're still like, it might not be me.
但你还是觉得，可能不是我。

936
00:46:21.840 --> 00:46:23.440
So, it kind of sounds like me.
所以，这听起来有点像我的风格。

937
00:46:23.540 --> 00:46:25.260
Although it also sounds like Mindy, too.
尽管听起来也有点像敏迪的。

938
00:46:25.920 --> 00:46:35.080
But this was intended to be originally a one-off joke gag in the delivery.
但最初这个设计本来只是个出场时的一性喜剧包袱。

939
00:46:35.440 --> 00:46:35.900
Yeah.
是啊。

940
00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:37.220
It hadn't been for more than that.
本来没打算搞那么大。

941
00:46:37.480 --> 00:46:37.840
Okay.
好吧。

942
00:46:37.940 --> 00:46:42.220
But it kind of grew as things do.
但就像很多事情一样，它慢慢发展壮大了。

943
00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:42.820
Yeah.
对啊。

944
00:46:42.820 --> 00:46:56.400
But I would like to note for the record, again, for the record, when conceived, this was simply a newspaper joke.
不过我想为历史作证，再次强调，就凭历史记录来看，在构思的时候，这真的只是个报纸笑话。

945
00:46:57.160 --> 00:46:57.980
Thank you.
谢谢你。

946
00:46:58.800 --> 00:46:59.920
Committed to record.
已记录在案。

947
00:47:00.420 --> 00:47:02.920
Angela, would you like to ask question number two?
安吉拉，你想问第二个问题吗？

948
00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:07.140
I would, and I don't think what you're commending to record proves anything, but okay.
我想问，而且我不认为你记录下来的东西能证明什么，不过好吧。

949
00:47:07.960 --> 00:47:08.500
Paul.
保罗。

950
00:47:08.920 --> 00:47:09.860
Yes, Angela.
在的，安吉拉。

951
00:47:10.120 --> 00:47:13.640
You are aware that people think Toby is the Scranton Strangler.
你知道大家觉得托比就是斯克兰顿扼喉杀手吗？

952
00:47:13.840 --> 00:47:14.160
Yes.
是的。

953
00:47:14.160 --> 00:47:22.700
So, Aiden B from the UK says, did Paul purposely write or play the role or plan for it to be as ambiguous as it is?
所以，来自英国的Aiden B问道，保罗是有意这样编写、诠释这个角色，还是计划让他的身份保持如此暧昧不清？

954
00:47:22.820 --> 00:47:24.780
Like, is Toby the Scranton Strangler?
也就是说，托比到底是斯克兰顿扼喉杀手吗？

955
00:47:25.120 --> 00:47:25.680
Yeah.
对。

956
00:47:25.800 --> 00:47:27.160
I'm curious about that, too.
我也很好奇这一点。

957
00:47:27.360 --> 00:47:34.800
When did you all become aware that fans were keying into Toby being the Scranton Strangler?
你们是什么时候发现粉丝们开始怀疑托比就是斯克兰顿扼喉杀手这一点的？

958
00:47:34.920 --> 00:47:36.460
Was it while we were still on the air?
是在我们还在播出的期间吗？

959
00:47:36.460 --> 00:47:37.680
It was after we wrapped.
是在我们杀青之后。

960
00:47:38.020 --> 00:47:44.820
So, I watched that YouTube video about, you know, putting together the very first one that said it might be Toby.
所以，我看过那个YouTube视频，你知道的，就是那部汇编了第一个指出可能是托比的视频。

961
00:47:45.040 --> 00:47:46.460
And that kind of blew my mind.
这让我觉得挺震撼的。

962
00:47:46.620 --> 00:47:47.600
There are many now.
现在这种视频有很多。

963
00:47:47.900 --> 00:47:48.700
Yeah, there are a lot.
对，有很多。

964
00:47:48.820 --> 00:47:51.500
So, and I watched a bunch for this podcaSt.
所以，为了这个播客我也看了不少。

965
00:47:52.060 --> 00:47:53.060
And they were long.
而且它们都很长。

966
00:47:55.820 --> 00:47:59.240
Because there's a lot of evidence to prove that he is.
因为有很多证据可以证明他就是。

967
00:47:59.240 --> 00:48:01.320
Yeah, well, and for other characters, too.
对，而且对其他角色也有这种说法。

968
00:48:01.480 --> 00:48:01.820
Right?
对吧？

969
00:48:02.660 --> 00:48:03.140
Yeah.
对。

970
00:48:03.420 --> 00:48:03.640
Yeah.
是的。

971
00:48:04.580 --> 00:48:08.780
Yes, for other characters that could be the Scranton Strangler.
对的，对于其他可能是斯克兰顿扼喉杀手的角色也有。

972
00:48:08.880 --> 00:48:10.360
There's a lot of YouTube out there.
油管上有各种各样的这种视频。

973
00:48:10.440 --> 00:48:10.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

974
00:48:11.920 --> 00:48:13.100
Pointing that out again.
再次指出了这一点。

975
00:48:15.180 --> 00:48:20.980
No, it had not crossed my mind that it could be, that it would be me.
不，我以前从来没想过可能是，会是我。

976
00:48:21.480 --> 00:48:24.560
We may have joked that it could be Cree.
我们可能开玩笑说可能是克里。

977
00:48:25.220 --> 00:48:27.020
We might have joked around like that.
我们当时可能会开这种玩笑。

978
00:48:27.020 --> 00:48:31.480
But Cree definitely had a lot of different lives that he led.
但克里确实过着许多种截然不同的生活。

979
00:48:31.720 --> 00:48:32.080
Yes.
是的。

980
00:48:32.700 --> 00:48:36.340
Yeah, which came out really strongly in season nine, I guess.
对，这在第九季里表现得非常明显，我猜。

981
00:48:36.420 --> 00:48:36.740
Yes.
没错。

982
00:48:38.220 --> 00:48:41.240
But that's the only, that's the kind of thing you could do in the very end.
但那是唯一，那是那种只有在快结束时才能做的事情。

983
00:48:41.640 --> 00:48:42.080
Right?
对吧？

984
00:48:42.220 --> 00:48:42.780
I guess.
我猜吧。

985
00:48:43.120 --> 00:48:43.280
Yeah.
是的。

986
00:48:43.660 --> 00:48:47.140
And Cree, I don't know, he existed on a whole different plane.
而且克里，我不知道，他完全生活在另一个维度的世界里。

987
00:48:47.280 --> 00:48:48.360
And he loves the idea.
而且他很喜欢这个主意。

988
00:48:48.580 --> 00:48:50.340
He loves the idea that he was the Scranton Strangler.
他很喜欢自己就是斯克兰顿扼喉杀手这个设定。

989
00:48:50.760 --> 00:48:54.700
And that Toby is the one everyone would pin it on, maybe, if not for George.
而且如果不是因为乔治的话，托比可能是大家都会把罪名安在他头上的人。

990
00:48:56.240 --> 00:48:58.960
Well, our next question is this.
好吧，我们的下一个问题是这样的。

991
00:48:59.380 --> 00:49:04.220
Mindy said that the Scranton Strangler was one of the most pitched things in the writer's room.
敏迪说过，斯克兰顿扼喉杀手是编剧室里被提出过最多创意的事情之一。

992
00:49:04.400 --> 00:49:10.020
She said that if you compiled all the notes, you would have an epic and terrifying miniseries.
她说如果你把所有的笔记整理起来，就能拍出一部史诗级且吓人的迷你剧。

993
00:49:10.260 --> 00:49:13.400
Do you remember any of the pitches that you guys had?
你们还记得当时你们想过哪些点子吗？

994
00:49:14.020 --> 00:49:19.360
No, I think it was a lot of just, this person gets strangled.
不，我觉得大部分都是，这个人被勒死了。

995
00:49:19.920 --> 00:49:23.600
You know, you're looking for, we're looking for twists in the story.
你知道的，你在寻找，我们在寻找故事中的转折。

996
00:49:23.760 --> 00:49:26.320
So like, we have this list up on the board, right?
所以就像，我们在白板上列了这样一个清单，对吧？

997
00:49:26.540 --> 00:49:31.240
Of like, after we write things, like, did we include inciting incident?
比如在我们写完东西之后，像，我们有没有包含引发事件？

998
00:49:32.280 --> 00:49:33.240
Oh, no.
哦，没有。

999
00:49:34.720 --> 00:49:39.080
You know, it's like, there's simple things in stories.
你知道的，就像故事里有一些很简单的事情。

1000
00:49:39.240 --> 00:49:40.820
And so one of them was a twiSt.
其中之一就是转折。

1001
00:49:41.060 --> 00:49:43.640
You know, is it a straight line to the end?
你知道的，这是笔直到尽头的直线吗？

1002
00:49:43.820 --> 00:49:46.620
Or, you know, do we go somewhere up with this?
还是说，你知道的，我们在这方面会有所提升吗？

1003
00:49:47.320 --> 00:49:53.120
So I think a twist or like second act break commonly could be somebody gets strangled.
所以我觉得一个反转或第二幕的转折通常可以是某人被勒住。

1004
00:49:54.220 --> 00:49:55.780
When we're really stretching.
当我们真的在勉强时。

1005
00:49:57.560 --> 00:49:58.400
All right.
好吧。

1006
00:49:58.560 --> 00:49:59.680
Next question, sir.
下一个问题，先生。

1007
00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.360
We also received a letter from Maria H.
我们还收到了一封来自玛丽亚·H.

1008
00:50:02.480 --> 00:50:04.160
in Atlanta, Georgia, who said,
佐治亚州亚特兰大的来信，她说，

1009
00:50:04.340 --> 00:50:08.580
have you heard the theory that the Scranton Strangler isn't a murderer?
你听说过斯克兰顿扼喉手其实不是杀人犯的理论吗？

1010
00:50:10.520 --> 00:50:16.220
Paul Lieberstein famously posted a video on Instagram a few years ago saying that the writers of the office
保罗·利伯斯坦几年前在Instagram上发过一个著名的视频，说《办公室》的编剧们

1011
00:50:16.220 --> 00:50:22.640
always intended to include that the Scranton Strangler would just strangle his victims till they passed out.
一直打算加入这样的情节：斯克兰顿扼喉手只是掐住受害者的脖子直到他们昏迷。

1012
00:50:22.640 --> 00:50:25.100
But never actually killed any of them.
但从来没有真正杀死过他们中的任何一个。

1013
00:50:25.680 --> 00:50:27.540
Now, I loved that.
现在，我很喜欢这个。

1014
00:50:27.840 --> 00:50:29.940
I thought that was super fun.
我觉得这超级有趣。

1015
00:50:30.160 --> 00:50:32.120
I'm not sure everybody was on board for that.
我不确定是不是所有人都赞同这一点。

1016
00:50:32.280 --> 00:50:34.140
But I loved it.
但我很喜欢。

1017
00:50:34.280 --> 00:50:36.640
Just like strangled you and left them there.
就像勒住你然后把你留在那里。

1018
00:50:37.280 --> 00:50:39.940
Such a weird, like, passive, violent crime.
这真是一种奇怪的、被动的暴力犯罪。

1019
00:50:40.260 --> 00:50:43.040
But very much, like, I could kill you, but I'm not going to.
但非常像是，我能杀了你，但我不会这么做。

1020
00:50:43.040 --> 00:50:43.920
It's weirder.
这就更奇怪了。

1021
00:50:43.920 --> 00:50:48.980
And then it becomes less of a, like, crazy thing.
然后它就变得不那么像是一件疯狂的事了。

1022
00:50:48.980 --> 00:50:51.140
I mean, it gets crazier.
我的意思是，这变得更疯狂了。

1023
00:50:51.140 --> 00:50:54.680
But in a way, it's just like, it's not a serial killer.
但在某种程度上，它就像是，这不是一个连环杀手。

1024
00:50:55.180 --> 00:50:55.400
Right.
对吧。

1025
00:50:55.620 --> 00:50:57.260
It's just a serial strangler.
这只是一个连环扼喉手。

1026
00:50:57.260 --> 00:51:02.400
It's just like, oh, that was a really bad night when I got strangled and passed out.
就像是，哦，那真是一个糟糕的夜晚，我被勒住然后昏迷了。

1027
00:51:02.740 --> 00:51:04.760
And then you live your life.
然后你继续生活。

1028
00:51:06.220 --> 00:51:08.080
You live the rest of your life.
你过着余下的生活。

1029
00:51:08.160 --> 00:51:08.920
And he knows.
而他知道。

1030
00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:09.300
He knows.
他知道。

1031
00:51:09.380 --> 00:51:10.320
Like, I'm going to take you to the edge.
就像是，我要把你逼到绝境。

1032
00:51:10.320 --> 00:51:10.980
It's just like, yeah.
这就好像是，是的。

1033
00:51:11.240 --> 00:51:11.320
Yeah.
是的。

1034
00:51:12.480 --> 00:51:13.140
But then poor George.
但可怜的乔治呢。

1035
00:51:13.140 --> 00:51:14.560
And it's like, okay, sure, that's traumatic.
这就好像是，好吧，当然，那是有创伤性的。

1036
00:51:14.980 --> 00:51:16.820
I'm not saying there wouldn't be some therapy.
我并不是说不需要做点心理咨询。

1037
00:51:16.820 --> 00:51:20.420
But it's like, it's so much smaller.
但这就好像是，这要小得多。

1038
00:51:20.740 --> 00:51:22.680
So this was just an idea in the writer's room.
所以这只是编剧室里的一个构思。

1039
00:51:22.820 --> 00:51:25.260
This never, this fact never shows up on the show.
这个从未、这个事实从未在剧中出现过。

1040
00:51:25.400 --> 00:51:25.620
It never shows up on the show.
它从未在剧中出现过。

1041
00:51:25.620 --> 00:51:26.280
This idea.
这个想法。

1042
00:51:26.500 --> 00:51:26.700
No.
没有。

1043
00:51:26.900 --> 00:51:27.220
Right.
对吧。

1044
00:51:27.340 --> 00:51:29.700
Which means it's not officially in the lore, yes.
这意味着它并没有官方计入背景设定中，是的。

1045
00:51:29.880 --> 00:51:36.020
And then also, too, that would contradict George Howard Scubb getting the death penalty
而且话说回来，那也会与乔治·霍华德·斯库布被判死刑

1046
00:51:36.020 --> 00:51:38.300
and life in prison, right?
和终身监禁相矛盾，对吧？

1047
00:51:38.300 --> 00:51:38.820
You're right.
你说得对。

1048
00:51:38.820 --> 00:51:40.840
Because you don't strangle someone.
因为你不会仅仅因为勒住某人而……

1049
00:51:41.940 --> 00:51:46.520
Your string of crimes, just stringing to passing out, doesn't get you death penalty.
你的犯罪行径，仅仅是勒到昏迷，是不会被判死刑的。

1050
00:51:47.060 --> 00:51:47.580
Yeah.
是的。

1051
00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:48.880
You're right.
你说得对。

1052
00:51:50.300 --> 00:51:51.320
Wow, Angela.
哇，安吉拉。

1053
00:51:51.840 --> 00:51:54.400
I feel like that is maybe.
我觉得也许是。

1054
00:51:54.760 --> 00:51:55.280
Unless.
除非。

1055
00:51:55.500 --> 00:51:55.760
What?
什么？

1056
00:51:56.100 --> 00:52:00.400
Unless he accidentally went too far one night and killed someone.
除非他有一天晚上不小心做得过火，杀了几个人。

1057
00:52:01.040 --> 00:52:01.560
Right.
对。

1058
00:52:02.360 --> 00:52:03.800
Okay, so maybe that happened.
好吧，所以也许真发生了。

1059
00:52:03.880 --> 00:52:04.660
Because you don't know what that.
因为你不知道那是什么。

1060
00:52:04.960 --> 00:52:05.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1061
00:52:05.600 --> 00:52:08.280
Well, this leads us to one of our last questions, Paul.
好吧，这就引出了我们的最后一个问题，保罗。

1062
00:52:08.280 --> 00:52:10.600
In our evidence gathering here.
在我们这里收集证据的过程中。

1063
00:52:10.920 --> 00:52:17.320
If you could go back and add one additional storyline for the Scranton Strangler, knowing
如果你能回到过去，为斯克兰顿扼杀魔增添一条额外的故事情节，结合

1064
00:52:17.320 --> 00:52:22.540
everything you know now about all of the fan interest, maybe it would wrap things up.
你现在对所有粉丝兴趣的了解，也许这能给事情一个了结。

1065
00:52:22.760 --> 00:52:24.000
Would you do it?
你会这么做吗？

1066
00:52:24.000 --> 00:52:25.880
And if so, what would that thing be?
如果是的话，那会是什么？

1067
00:52:26.520 --> 00:52:28.480
No, I probably wouldn't wrap it up for the audience.
不，我可能不会给观众一个了结。

1068
00:52:28.740 --> 00:52:31.680
But Scubb getting out of prison, like say we had gone another 10 years.
但斯卡布出狱了，比如我们再拍10年。

1069
00:52:31.880 --> 00:52:32.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1070
00:52:32.340 --> 00:52:32.660
Okay.
好吧。

1071
00:52:32.700 --> 00:52:32.760
You know.
你知道的。

1072
00:52:33.320 --> 00:52:36.220
With Scubb maybe getting out of prison and.
比如斯卡布出狱然后。

1073
00:52:36.540 --> 00:52:40.180
Would Scubb become Toby's friend that he'd always hoped for?
斯卡布会成为托比一直希望成为的朋友吗？

1074
00:52:40.180 --> 00:52:42.680
Or Toby could be very, very scared.
或者托比会感到非常非常害怕。

1075
00:52:44.020 --> 00:52:48.180
You know, or members of the jury could be very scared.
你知道的，或者陪审团成员会非常害怕。

1076
00:52:48.420 --> 00:52:53.660
Or there could be another strangling while Scubb was in prison.
或者在斯卡布入狱期间还会发生另一起谋杀案。

1077
00:52:53.860 --> 00:52:55.900
Well, that would definitely fuel the fire.
嗯，那绝对会火上浇油。

1078
00:52:56.200 --> 00:52:56.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1079
00:52:56.780 --> 00:52:59.800
And was it a copycat or did they get the wrong guy?
那是模仿作案还是他们抓错人了？

1080
00:53:01.000 --> 00:53:02.120
Interesting questions.
有趣的问题。

1081
00:53:02.620 --> 00:53:02.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1082
00:53:03.460 --> 00:53:04.660
We would do something like that.
我们会做类似的事情。

1083
00:53:05.060 --> 00:53:05.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1084
00:53:05.700 --> 00:53:06.940
It would have continued.
它会延续下去。

1085
00:53:07.220 --> 00:53:08.000
Yeah, for sure.
是的，肯定的。

1086
00:53:08.100 --> 00:53:08.700
If we had continued.
如果我们继续拍下去的话。

1087
00:53:09.440 --> 00:53:11.680
The Scranton Strangler case was not over.
斯克兰顿扼杀魔案并没有结束。

1088
00:53:12.220 --> 00:53:12.700
No.
没有。

1089
00:53:12.860 --> 00:53:14.780
Something like that isn't over ever.
这样的事永远不会结束。

1090
00:53:15.320 --> 00:53:15.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1091
00:53:15.740 --> 00:53:18.020
We're still talking about the Menendez brothers.
我们现在还在讨论梅嫩德斯兄弟呢。

1092
00:53:18.720 --> 00:53:19.120
True.
确实。

