What?
什么？

1187
00:56:50.400 --> 00:56:50.480
Cassie?
卡茜？

1188
00:56:50.480 --> 00:56:51.340
No, definitely never.
不，绝对不可能。

1189
00:56:51.340 --> 00:56:52.620
Cassie's raising her hand.
卡茜在举手。

1190
00:56:52.740 --> 00:56:56.900
Angela, I want to give you props for like your debate, even though you loSt.
安吉拉，我想称赞你一下你的辩论，尽管你输了。

1191
00:56:57.100 --> 00:57:00.340
There was something you brought up that I kept thinking about.
你提到的一件事让我一直在想。

1192
00:57:00.340 --> 00:57:08.700
And you said that when George is driving the getaway car, that car had been parked in the Dunder Mifflin parking lot before.
你说当乔治开着逃跑的车时，那辆车之前曾停在邓德米夫林的停车场里。

1193
00:57:09.320 --> 00:57:11.040
Of course, that's a production thing.
当然，那是制作方面的原因。

1194
00:57:11.040 --> 00:57:17.020
But in the world of Scranton, I think that would be grounds for him to have an appeal.
但在斯克兰顿的世界里，我认为这足以成为他提出上诉的理由。

1195
00:57:17.540 --> 00:57:18.820
Because what is that about?
因为那是怎么回事？

1196
00:57:19.420 --> 00:57:19.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1197
00:57:19.880 --> 00:57:22.240
