00:59:52.880 --> 00:59:53.940
Paul, I took an online course.
保罗，我报了个网课。

1250
00:59:54.100 --> 00:59:55.120
I'm certified now.
我现在有结业证了。

1251
00:59:55.380 --> 00:59:55.980
I am certified.
我有证书。

1252
00:59:56.240 --> 00:59:57.580
Do you see a jury in this room?
你在这个房间里看到陪审团了吗？

1253
00:59:57.700 --> 00:59:58.060
I do.
看到了。

1254
00:59:59.140 --> 01:00:00.180
Sam and Cassie.
山姆和卡茜。

1255
01:00:01.580 --> 01:00:04.080
Yeah, Cassie, I am curious.
对，卡茜，我很好奇。

1256
01:00:05.080 --> 01:00:10.880
Before Paul gave us the definitive answer and I won because I picked the right side,
在保罗给出最终定论、而我因为选对了边获胜之前，

1257
01:00:10.880 --> 01:00:15.400
who were you going to award the win to based on our debating?
根据我们的辩论，你原本打算把胜出判给谁？

1258
01:00:15.940 --> 01:00:18.640
Yeah, you both had great arguments and everything.
对，你们两个的论点都很棒之类的。

1259
01:00:18.760 --> 01:00:24.620
I do think Angela had the hardest job, but yeah, I would have given it to you, Jenna, because-
我确实觉得安吉拉的任务最艰巨，但是吧，我本来会把胜利判给你，珍娜，因为——

1260
01:00:24.620 --> 01:00:25.100
To me?
给我？

1261
01:00:25.240 --> 01:00:25.480
Oh!
噢！

1262
01:00:25.640 --> 01:00:28.120
I don't think Toby is the Scranton Strangler.
我不觉得托比是斯克兰顿扼喉手。

1263
01:00:28.500 --> 01:00:29.800
I will also say this.
我还要说这个。

1264
01:00:29.920 --> 01:00:34.740
Jenna proudly said, because I picked the right argument, we just said we both have to pick
珍娜骄傲地说，因为我选对了论点，我们刚刚说过我们俩都得选

1265
01:00:34.740 --> 01:00:35.100
one.
一个。

1266
01:00:35.540 --> 01:00:36.220
What do you want to do?
你想怎么做？

1267
01:00:36.580 --> 01:00:38.980
And Jenna was like, I'll say that he isn't.
然后珍娜就说，我会说他不是。

1268
01:00:39.000 --> 01:00:39.700
I said, okay, fine.
我说，好吧，行。

1269
01:00:41.040 --> 01:00:48.460
Well, and I want to say I might have been awarded the win by both Paul and Cassie, but
嗯，而且我想说，我可能赢得了保罗和卡茜的认可，但

1270
01:00:48.460 --> 01:00:55.100
I would have awarded you the win because I thought your debate was just fantastic today.
我会把胜利判给你，因为我觉得你今天的辩论实在是太精彩了。

1271
01:00:55.560 --> 01:00:57.020
I really, really did.
我是真的、真的很这么觉得。

1272
01:00:57.020 --> 01:01:00.740
I was like, oh no, I was sweating it when it was my turn.
我当时就想，哦不，轮到我的时候我直冒冷汗。

1273
01:01:01.740 --> 01:01:03.940
So I feel like we both won today.
所以我觉得我们今天都赢了。

1274
01:01:04.060 --> 01:01:05.240
And you know who I really think won?
而且你知道我真心觉得谁赢了吗？

1275
01:01:05.460 --> 01:01:06.520
The Office Ladies community.
《办公室女士》的粉丝社区。

1276
01:01:06.740 --> 01:01:07.640
Oh yeah, for sure.
哦对，绝对是的。

1277
01:01:08.440 --> 01:01:09.320
Really, really.
真的，真的。

1278
01:01:09.320 --> 01:01:11.320
And Paul, you're in studio with us.
保罗，你和我们在录音室里。

1279
01:01:11.320 --> 01:01:12.340
This is so fun.
这太有趣了。

1280
01:01:12.540 --> 01:01:13.040
I know, this is so great.
我知道，这太棒了。

1281
01:01:13.580 --> 01:01:19.300
Before you go, can you tell us about your project with Audible, your show, Middle Space?
在你离开之前，能给我们讲讲你和 Audible 合作的项目、你的节目《中间空间》吗？

1282
01:01:19.460 --> 01:01:20.300
Oh yeah, I love this thing so much.
哦对，我太喜欢这个了。

1283
01:01:20.300 --> 01:01:21.840
I want people to listen to it.
我希望大家去听听看。

1284
01:01:21.900 --> 01:01:25.420
I want people to, as well, Middle Space, all one word.
我也希望大家去听，中间空间，连在一起的。

1285
01:01:25.560 --> 01:01:31.340
But the full title is Middle Space, colon, The Rebels Attack, and then The Other Side Attacks
但完整的标题是《中间空间：叛军进攻》，还有《另一方进攻》

1286
01:01:31.340 --> 01:01:31.780
as well.
也是。

1287
01:01:33.480 --> 01:01:37.840
And it is one of the funnest, silliest things I've ever done.
这是我做过最好玩、最滑稽的事情之一。

1288
01:01:38.100 --> 01:01:40.160
Will you tell us sort of the world of it?
你能给我们大致讲讲它的世界观吗？

1289
01:01:40.360 --> 01:01:40.800
Yes.
可以。

1290
01:01:40.980 --> 01:01:42.480
So we're in space.
我们在太空中。

1291
01:01:42.740 --> 01:01:43.120
Okay.
好的。

1292
01:01:43.280 --> 01:01:45.020
Let's call it the future, I guess.
我们就叫它未来吧，我想。

1293
01:01:45.900 --> 01:01:48.960
And Will Forte stars as this captain.
威尔·福特饰演这个船长。

1294
01:01:49.120 --> 01:01:50.140
He's so funny.
他太搞笑了。

1295
01:01:50.520 --> 01:01:57.640
Who starts off very early that they get a distress call and he decides not to go.
一开场没多久，他们就收到了求救信号，而他决定不去。

1296
01:01:58.140 --> 01:01:59.800
Oh, not to take the distress call.
哦，不理会求救信号。

1297
01:01:59.800 --> 01:02:00.340
Not to go.
不去。

1298
01:02:00.660 --> 01:02:01.380
Doesn't feel like it.
感觉不想去。

1299
01:02:01.380 --> 01:02:03.020
But he doesn't feel like it.
但他就是不想去。

1300
01:02:03.120 --> 01:02:04.060
He doesn't want to.
他不想去。

1301
01:02:04.320 --> 01:02:04.880
Okay.
好吧。

1302
01:02:05.300 --> 01:02:06.220
And that's his reason.
这就是他的理由。

1303
01:02:06.380 --> 01:02:07.300
He just doesn't want to.
他就是不想去。

1304
01:02:07.460 --> 01:02:09.380
And he's that kind of captain.
而且他就是那种船长。

1305
01:02:10.600 --> 01:02:13.700
And he just kind of wants to float around in space.
他只想在太空中四处漂浮。

1306
01:02:13.700 --> 01:02:19.720
And he's very interested in getting out of the space business, captaining business.
他对退出太空行业、船长行业非常感兴趣。

1307
01:02:19.780 --> 01:02:21.820
He'd like to get into fast food.
他想涉足快餐业。

1308
01:02:23.080 --> 01:02:29.060
And goes around interviewing a manager of an intergalactic burger chain.
于是到处去采访一个星际汉堡连锁店的经理。

1309
01:02:29.880 --> 01:02:34.580
But it is, you know, four and a half hours of not a single mission.
但你知道，那是足足四个半小时没有任何任务的剧情。

1310
01:02:34.660 --> 01:02:36.640
It's just life in space.
这只是太空中的生活。

1311
01:02:38.500 --> 01:02:41.980
And it's very, like, anti-sci-fi.
而且非常反科幻。

1312
01:02:42.780 --> 01:02:44.340
Oh, Jenna, you might like it.
哦，珍娜，你可能会喜欢它。

1313
01:02:44.480 --> 01:02:50.480
I am not a sci-fi fan, but I love this comedy spin on sci-fi.
我不是科幻迷，但我很喜欢这种对科幻的喜剧恶搞。

1314
01:02:50.880 --> 01:02:54.780
Like, it's a satirical take on sci-fi adventure.
就像是对科幻冒险的讽刺性戏仿。

1315
01:02:54.980 --> 01:02:55.640
I have a question.
我有个问题。

1316
01:02:55.640 --> 01:02:56.300
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

1317
01:02:56.460 --> 01:02:57.320
It's a great caSt.
演员阵容很强大。

1318
01:02:57.660 --> 01:02:58.840
John Malkovich narrated.
约翰·马尔科维奇担任旁白。

1319
01:02:59.060 --> 01:02:59.920
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1320
01:02:59.980 --> 01:03:02.900
And we had a lot of great people in there.
里面有很多优秀的演员。

1321
01:03:03.120 --> 01:03:04.400
I have one question.
我有一个问题。

1322
01:03:04.700 --> 01:03:04.880
Yeah.
对。

1323
01:03:05.500 --> 01:03:12.780
Throughout the whole time where he's looking at how to become a fast food worker, are there
在他研究如何成为一名快餐店员工的整个过程中，有没有

1324
01:03:12.780 --> 01:03:16.140
more distress calls that come through that he just continues to ignore?
更多的求救信号传过来而他却一直置之不理？

1325
01:03:16.280 --> 01:03:16.600
Yes.
有的。

1326
01:03:16.820 --> 01:03:18.240
He ignores all work.
他对所有工作都置之不理。

1327
01:03:21.060 --> 01:03:26.000
They would like to mutiny, but they're not quite capable of pulling that off because that
他们很想哗变，但他们没有能力付诸行动，因为那

1328
01:03:26.000 --> 01:03:26.680
takes a lot.
需要付出很多。

1329
01:03:26.820 --> 01:03:27.700
It takes a lot of effort.
需要付出很大的努力。

1330
01:03:27.820 --> 01:03:28.100
Yeah.
是的。

1331
01:03:28.520 --> 01:03:29.980
I mean, you got to kill someone.
我的意思是，你得杀个人。

1332
01:03:30.240 --> 01:03:32.160
They don't want to do that in the end.
到头来他们并不想这么做。

1333
01:03:33.900 --> 01:03:39.900
He might listen to Mel Robbins, who likes to remind us all the time that I don't want to
他可能会听梅尔·罗宾斯的播客，梅尔总是提醒我们，“我不想去”

1334
01:03:39.900 --> 01:03:43.260
is a perfectly acceptable reason to not do something.
是一个完全可以接受的不做某事的理由。

1335
01:03:43.500 --> 01:03:44.280
To not do something.
不做某事。

1336
01:03:45.280 --> 01:03:46.620
And reigns in it.
并沉浸其中。

1337
01:03:46.720 --> 01:03:49.320
And he plays the rebel leader.
而且他饰演叛军领袖。

1338
01:03:49.820 --> 01:03:50.800
Oh, great.
哦，太棒了。

1339
01:03:51.280 --> 01:03:56.500
And he has – he calls up – one of the people on the ship is in contact with the rebel leader.
而且他——他打电话——船上的一个人与叛军领袖有联系。

1340
01:03:56.640 --> 01:03:56.860
Clark.
克拉克。

1341
01:03:57.080 --> 01:03:57.740
Clark Duke is in it.
克拉克·杜克参演了。

1342
01:03:57.740 --> 01:03:58.980
Oh, Clark is in it.
哦，克拉克演了。

1343
01:03:58.980 --> 01:04:03.900
And Clark plays the – someone on the bridge who's very upset that we're not –
克拉克饰演——舰桥上的某个人，对我们没有——感到非常沮丧

1344
01:04:03.900 --> 01:04:05.320
Taking the distress calls?
接听求救信号？

1345
01:04:05.480 --> 01:04:07.260
Taking the distress calls or really doing anything.
接听求救信号或者真正做点什么。

1346
01:04:07.320 --> 01:04:07.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1347
01:04:07.760 --> 01:04:11.260
You know, who doesn't know what his life's about if he's not doing something.
你知道，如果什么都不做，他甚至不知道自己的人生是为了什么。

1348
01:04:11.980 --> 01:04:17.380
So he gets in contact with the rebel leader and he calls him up and his son answers.
所以他联系了叛军领袖，给他打电话，结果是他儿子接的电话。

1349
01:04:19.100 --> 01:04:21.200
And they have a great conversation.
他们进行了一场精彩的对话。

1350
01:04:21.220 --> 01:04:24.460
And it's played by Henry, my son.
而那个角色由亨利饰演，也就是我儿子。

1351
01:04:24.640 --> 01:04:25.100
Aw.
噢。

1352
01:04:25.100 --> 01:04:28.600
And we did it kind of like word by word.
而且我们差不多是一个词一个词地录的。

1353
01:04:28.600 --> 01:04:30.140
He was really young at the time.
他那时候真的很年轻。

1354
01:04:30.400 --> 01:04:30.820
Aw.
噢。

1355
01:04:30.920 --> 01:04:32.000
And it's so cute.
而且真的好可爱。

1356
01:04:32.260 --> 01:04:33.360
And it's so funny.
而且真的好搞笑。

1357
01:04:33.580 --> 01:04:35.340
I can't wait to hear that, Paul.
保罗，我等不及想听听那个了。

1358
01:04:35.500 --> 01:04:36.440
Oh, I love that.
哦，我太喜欢那个了。

1359
01:04:36.700 --> 01:04:37.040
Yeah.
对。

1360
01:04:37.480 --> 01:04:41.960
Well, we'll include all the information in our Insta stories and our website with links
好的，我们会在Ins快拍和官网上附上所有信息和链接

1361
01:04:41.960 --> 01:04:43.380
so you guys can go and listen.
这样你们就可以去收听了。

1362
01:04:43.820 --> 01:04:44.920
That is so cool.
太酷了。

1363
01:04:45.180 --> 01:04:47.380
And then, Paul, just one last thing.
那么，保罗，还有最后一件事。

1364
01:04:47.620 --> 01:04:52.160
You know, we've put a period at the end of the sentence of one fan theory.
你知道的，我们刚刚给某个粉丝理论画上了句号。

1365
01:04:52.480 --> 01:04:52.680
Yeah.
对。

1366
01:04:52.680 --> 01:04:57.900
And I hate to open a window here on another.
但我又不想挑起另一个话题。

1367
01:04:58.200 --> 01:04:59.780
Oh, I see what you did there.
哦，我懂你刚才那个双关梗。

1368
01:05:00.120 --> 01:05:08.100
But the last time we saw you, we discussed your particular pet peeve, which is that the
但上次见到你时，我们讨论了你的一大死穴，那就是

1369
01:05:08.100 --> 01:05:14.120
windows of the Dunder Mifflin building, the interior and exterior windows do not match.
邓德米弗林大楼的窗户，室内和室外的窗户根本对不上。

1370
01:05:14.280 --> 01:05:14.460
Yes.
是的。

1371
01:05:14.600 --> 01:05:16.140
Would you like a moment to speak to that?
你想借此机会发表一下高见吗？

1372
01:05:16.240 --> 01:05:16.760
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

1373
01:05:16.880 --> 01:05:18.620
Because you're very passionate about this.
因为你对此真的满腔热情。

1374
01:05:18.620 --> 01:05:18.960
I am.
我是。

1375
01:05:19.060 --> 01:05:20.380
This bugged me so much.
这事快把我烦死了。

1376
01:05:20.440 --> 01:05:22.960
And no one seemed to care at all.
而且好像根本没人介意。

1377
01:05:23.560 --> 01:05:23.940
Let's...
让我们……

1378
01:05:23.940 --> 01:05:24.700
Paul, here is this.
保罗，这个给你。

1379
01:05:24.720 --> 01:05:26.380
Paul, this is your radon.
保罗，这就是你的氡气。

1380
01:05:26.420 --> 01:05:27.740
This is your radon.
这就是你的氡气。

1381
01:05:28.220 --> 01:05:31.340
What radon was to Toby these windows are to you.
托比有多讨厌氡气，你就有多讨厌这些窗户。

1382
01:05:31.520 --> 01:05:34.620
So we set the windows, obviously, in Culver City, right?
所以我们最初的布景在卡尔弗城，对吧？

1383
01:05:34.820 --> 01:05:38.260
When we were down there, we moved to the valley in season two.
当我们还在那儿的时候，我们在第二季搬到了山谷。

1384
01:05:38.440 --> 01:05:38.680
Right.
没错。

1385
01:05:38.680 --> 01:05:43.280
Outside of that building had those big, wide glass things.
那个建筑外面有那种又大又宽的玻璃。

1386
01:05:43.520 --> 01:05:50.540
And then the inside of our windows were these very small, kind of like three by six rectangular
然后我们室内的窗户却是那种非常小的、大概三乘六的矩形

1387
01:05:50.540 --> 01:05:51.080
windows.
窗户。

1388
01:05:51.960 --> 01:05:53.360
There's no way they match.
它们绝对不可能对得上。

1389
01:05:53.560 --> 01:05:55.100
I mean, it's startling.
我是说，这太显眼了。

1390
01:05:57.840 --> 01:06:05.280
And then the view from anybody's, any one window, we would change all the time, depending
然后从任何人的窗户看出去的风景，我们随时都在变，取决于

1391
01:06:05.280 --> 01:06:06.500
on what we wanted to see.
我们当时想看到什么。

1392
01:06:06.740 --> 01:06:07.380
That's true.
确实如此。

1393
01:06:07.600 --> 01:06:09.920
And that pissed me off so much, too.
而且这也把我气得够呛。

1394
01:06:10.080 --> 01:06:13.040
It's just like, no, out that window has to be this one thing.
就好像，不行，那个窗户外面必须是那个特定的景物。

1395
01:06:13.240 --> 01:06:15.020
And they're like, nope, it doesn't matter.
但他们却说，不，这不重要。

1396
01:06:15.220 --> 01:06:15.920
And it doesn't matter.
而且这确实不重要。

1397
01:06:16.060 --> 01:06:17.340
And then I broke it, too.
然后我还把它给打破了。

1398
01:06:17.460 --> 01:06:20.060
And we needed to kind of like see Michael hop a train.
当时我们需要看到迈克尔去赶火车之类的。

1399
01:06:20.500 --> 01:06:23.220
I picked that window to be outside, you know.
我挑了那个窗户作为室外视角，你懂的。

1400
01:06:26.380 --> 01:06:27.160
That's great.
太棒了。

1401
01:06:28.360 --> 01:06:28.760
Yeah.
没错。

1402
01:06:29.000 --> 01:06:30.260
You're part of the problem.
你也是问题的一部分。

1403
01:06:30.600 --> 01:06:31.220
I'm part of the problem.
我也是问题的一部分。

1404
01:06:32.280 --> 01:06:35.660
Well, do you feel any better now that you've at least gotten to speak to it?
好吧，既然你至少已经跟它说上话了，现在有没有感觉好一点？

1405
01:06:36.040 --> 01:06:39.720
I think at one point I was like, let's not, don't point the camera up.
我想我曾经有一刻觉得，算了吧，别把镜头往上抬。

1406
01:06:40.440 --> 01:06:42.120
Don't see the windows in the building.
别拍大楼里的窗户。

1407
01:06:42.440 --> 01:06:43.200
Just keep it low.
镜头压低点就行。

1408
01:06:43.980 --> 01:06:45.300
People are going to freak out.
人们会抓狂的。

1409
01:06:45.660 --> 01:06:46.720
It's not going to be okay.
情况不会好转的。

1410
01:06:46.860 --> 01:06:47.940
It's not the same windows.
那不是同一扇窗户。

1411
